I just realized that SNAP.COM is very very short -- I should have just
posted it in the first place.  To use, uudecode, then run once only
(per dos boot) to install.  Alt-Enter takes a picture of the current
text screen and saves it.  Ctrl-Enter overwrites the current screen with
the saved one.  Ctrl-Alt-Enter swaps the saved and current screens.  By
doing Ctrl-Alt-Enter twice, you can peek at the saved screen without
messing up the current screen.

What I do is take a picture of some legitimate-looking screen, then start
nethacking.  When someone walks too close -- POW!  I hit Ctrl-Enter.
When it is again safe, I hit ^R, so nethack redraws.  I could also have
simply hit Ctrl-Alt-Enter twice, but in an emergency, Ctrl-Enter is so
much harder to mess up!  In fact, I have a hacked-up version (not included)
where you can just hit the '+' key on the number pad to do the same as Ctrl-
Enter.  That affords +3 stealth!

